//  Set the SDL error message for the current thread. Calling this function will replace any
//   previous error message that was set. This function always returns false, since SDL frequently
//   uses false to signify a failing result, leading to this idiom: ```c if (error_code) { return
//   SDL_SetError("This operation has failed: %d", error_code); } ```
